MC Player Agent is an independent derivative project, not an official Numen release.

Portions are adapted from Numen (minecraft-numen) by Dwinovo and contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/Dwinovo/minecraft-numen
Original code license: LGPL-3.0-only. See LICENSE and COPYING.
Changes made on 2026-10-28: player-agent extraction, independent runtime and
model transport, new loader entrypoints, own branding/storage and legacy migration.
Per-file source paths and original SHA-256 values are recorded in provenance.json.
Numen artwork, character assets, voices and branding are not included.

The unmodified Gradle wrapper is distributed under Apache-2.0; see licenses/.
Minecraft, Fabric, NeoForge and Gson remain their respective upstream projects.

Provenance clarification (2026-10-28): of the 61 extracted files recorded in
provenance.json, 57 are absent from the original local Numen download and were
introduced during the local player-agent development work. They must not all
be attributed as pre-existing upstream Numen implementations. Four origin files
exist in that snapshot: DigTime, RecipeProbe, ItemReach and ItemEntityDropsMixin.
Presence of a file does not mean all extracted methods originated upstream;
player pickup receipt hooks and centre-based pickup checks were local additions.
This snapshot comparison does not establish exclusive authorship. LGPL notices
and actual upstream attribution are retained. New mission subsystem files are
implemented in the independent MC Player Agent project.

Harness maintenance (2026-10-28): AgentHarness extracts and adapts scheduling,
review, interruption and completion logic from this project's PlayerControl.
This is a continuation of the recorded local player-agent implementation, not
a claim of newly originating all scheduling logic. The headless demo and new
harness tests are added in this independent project. Existing notices remain.

Harness maintenance (2026-10-29): per-session time, model-request and action
limits, boundary regression tests and public project documentation were added
with AI-assisted development. Existing upstream attribution is unchanged.
